  "id": "COMPOUND:14989 - PROTEIN:5677",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but interconnected pathway linking the compound in question to JM1. The compound is directly targeted by CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which in turn is targeted by 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide. This latter compound has JM1 as its target, establishing a direct link between the compound and JM1 through a series of enzymatic interactions. Additionally, the compound is also targeted by another enzyme, (1S,3E,4S,5S,6S)-4,5-dihydroxy-3-(3-methylbut-2-enylidene)-7-oxabicyclo[4.1.0]heptan-2-one, which also leads to JM1. These findings collectively suggest that the compound may act as a modulator or inhibitor of JM1 through a series of enzymatic pathways, potentially influencing its biological activity. The evidence supports a mechanism where the compound interacts with multiple enzymes, ultimately affecting JM1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
